hey this is presto Walker reminding you  to mind your decisions a car averages 75  miles per hour downhill 60 miles per  hour on flat roads and 50 miles per hour  uphill it takes three hours to go from  town a to town B and it takes three  hours and 30 minutes for the return  journey by the same route what is the  distance between towns a and B a similar  and perhaps easier version of this  problem was asked in a US Math Olympiad  qualifying test I adapted this problem  from the website cubit org pause the  video if you'd like to give this problem  a try and when you're ready keep  watching to learn how to solve this  problem  [Music]  so how can we figure out the distance  between towns a and B let's first write  an equation for the time it takes to go  from A to B the time it takes to go from  A to B will be the sum of three  different times it'll be the time  downhill plus the amount of time on flat  roads plus the amount of time uphill we  can express each of these times as the  ratio of the distance divided by the  speed we can then substitute in the  downhill flat and uphill speeds which  are given in the problem and we'll let  the distances be denoted by unknown  variables we know this time from A to B  is a total of 3 hours so now how do we  write a similar equation going from B to  a well notice that if you're going  uphill from A to B it'll be downhill  going from B to a similarly if you're  going downhill from A to B it'll be  uphill going from B to a the flat roads  will be the same on either one-way  journey so to get the time from B to a  we're going to swap the variables D and  u and this will be a total of 3.5 hours  so we now have two equations but we have  three variables so we can't solve for  each variable explicitly but we don't  need to we only need to solve for the  distance between the towns which is the  sum of DF and you how can we do that  well we're going to do a neat little  trick and sum the two equations so we  add the second equation to the first  let's line up these variables and then  let's add each column the first column  becomes 5d over 150 then 2f over 60 then  5u over 150 and the sum of these is 6.5  we can then simplify each of these  fractions to be 1 over 30 and we now  have one equation we multiply both sides  by 30 and we get rid of these  denominators and we get D plus F Plus u  is equal to 6 point 5 times 30  which is equal to 195 miles and like  magic we have solved for the distance  between town a and town B and the answer  is 195 miles thanks for watching and for  making mind your decisions one of the  best channels on YouTube banks are  watching and thanks for your support  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

